  "title": "XML: Use libxml2 function instead of struct elements directly",
  "description": "xmlValidPotentialChildren gets the list of potential children exactly\nas a we want, without having to access internal struct members. (We\nhave to impose a maximum limit, but that's ok and it has the virtue\nof limiting the recursion.)\n\nBoth this function and accessing the struct members were deprecated\nin libxml2-2.15.0, but this function has been undeprecated for the\nnext release.\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 648b1603f6d7c6a21e4fde11dc6a82febcf79c14)\n\nCo-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>",
